                <pb facs="0861" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/185: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-20T16:00:00+08:00">November 20, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 21—2:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1012. My 1010, November 19, 7 p.m., paragraph 3. Following from American Consul
                    at Nanking: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 19, 8 p.m. Japanese Consul General at Shanghai has just
                            informed me that he had a conversation today with Minister for Foreign
                            Affairs urging latter to permit Japanese representatives to participate
                            in Provisional Court negotiations but that Wang declined to do so.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
